<p>Five European governments — the UK, France, Germany, Sweden and the Netherlands — say lab analysis of samples taken from the late Russian opposition leader Alexei Navalny “conclusively confirmed” the presence of epibatidine, a potent neurotoxin linked to South American poison dart frogs. The governments say there is “no innocent explanation” for the substance turning up, and argue it undercuts Russia’s earlier claim that Navalny died of natural causes while imprisoned in a remote Arctic penal colony in 2024. The five countries said they will take the case to the Organisation for the Prohibition of Chemical Weapons, alleging a breach of the Chemical Weapons Convention. Russia rejected the accusations and demanded evidence, calling the claims propaganda.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Z6W4gS8wtgG1GNySknIOikYTQK3-REmj7u_diESOvHC5UtYZ7j4mO-G9tenPWfpaMm4mrLZA_zZNUXIRvhU9vJjEQGW-0ne2lgpVbB0jO8XSnKxdpS1389YnKyHZYIzI5Y17pdXpD8miwzB7xokYMejEiqblyX33Bx_AzRczru9FCExAcHlnwNjzoo0' alt='Aleksei A. Navalny in Moscow in 2014, when he was a leading Putin critic.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Why epibatidine stood out: Meduza said epibatidine accumulates in the skin of Epipedobates frogs native to Ecuador and Peru, while the joint statement noted that dart frogs kept in captivity do not produce the toxin.</li><li>How samples moved: Meduza reported that biological samples linked to Navalny were smuggled out of Russia before testing.</li><li>European assessment language: Euronews reported that the five governments argued only the Russian state had the means and motive to carry out the poisoning, using language that included “contempt for international law”.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Five European governments: Said European lab tests detected epibatidine in samples linked to Navalny, argued the toxin does not occur naturally in Russia, and said they will raise the matter with the OPCW under the Chemical Weapons Convention framework. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/russia-poisoned-opposition-leader-alexei-navalny-with-dart-frog-toxin-five-european-nations-say'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Russian government: Russian officials dismissed the allegations, demanded evidence, and described the claims as propaganda or a hoax. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/14/russias-alexey-navalny-killed-by-dart-frog-poison-european-nations-allege'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>Yulia Navalnaya: Navalny’s widow backed the poisoning finding and called President Vladimir Putin a “murderer,” according to Firstpost’s report on her reaction. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/yulia-navalnaya-react-to-european-poison-claim-alexei-navalny-death-putin-murder-russia-13979912.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Meduza (independent Russian outlet): Meduza focused on what epibatidine is, why human exposure is rare, and how its effects can resemble nicotine poisoning at certain doses. (<a href='https://meduza.io/en/cards/what-is-epibatidine-and-how-did-it-kill-navalny-a-guide-to-the-frog-neurotoxin-that-five-countries-say-poisoned-russia-s-opposition-leader'>Meduza</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/14/world/europe/russia-navalny-poison.html'>Navalny Was Poisoned With Frog Toxin, European Governments Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3343599/russia-poisoned-alexei-navalny-dart-frog-toxin-european-nations-say'>Russia poisoned Alexei Navalny with dart frog toxin, European nations say</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/14/russia-poisoned-navalny-according-to-five-european-countries-scientific-findings'>Russia poisoned Navalny, according to five European countries&#x27; scientific findings</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/14/russias-alexey-navalny-killed-by-dart-frog-poison-european-nations-allege'>Russia’s Alexey Navalny killed by dart frog poison, European nations allege</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://time.com/7378735/navalny-poison-frog-toxin-russia/'>Russian Opposition Leader Navalny Poisoned With Deadly ‘Dart Frog’ Toxin, European Governments Say</a> - time.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/european-allies-say-navalny-was-poisoned-by-dart-frog-toxin-russia-rejects-claims'>European allies say Navalny was poisoned by dart frog toxin; Russia rejects claims</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/russia-poisoned-opposition-leader-alexei-navalny-with-dart-frog-toxin-five-european-nations-say'>Russia poisoned opposition leader Alexei Navalny with dart frog toxin, five European nations say</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/cards/what-is-epibatidine-and-how-did-it-kill-navalny-a-guide-to-the-frog-neurotoxin-that-five-countries-say-poisoned-russia-s-opposition-leader'>What is epibatidine, and how did it kill Navalny? A guide to the frog neurotoxin that five countries say poisoned Russia’s opposition leader.</a> - meduza.io</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwyk4lz4e3eo'>Russia killed opposition leader Alexei Navalny using dart frog toxin, UK says</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/inside-the-dart-frog-toxin-reportedly-linked-to-alexei-navalnys-death-11004464#publisher=newsstand'>Inside The &#x27;Dart Frog Toxin&#x27; Reportedly Linked To Alexei Navalny&#x27;s Death</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/yulia-navalnaya-react-to-european-poison-claim-alexei-navalny-death-putin-murder-russia-13979912.html'>&#x27;I was certain from first day&#x27;: Alexei Navalny&#x27;s wife calls Putin &#x27;murderer&#x27; after poisoning claim</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nbcnews.com/world/russia/russian-opposition-leader-alexei-navalny-poisoned-deadly-dart-frog-rcna259064'>France, Germany, the Netherlands, Sweden, and the United Kingdom assess that Russian op